System 573: per-voice SPU attenuation + SPU register-write snoop ("573 Announcer/Crowd").

2026-10-30. An OSD convenience, not hardware behaviour: during a DDR song the SPU
plays only the announcer and the crowd (MAME reference runs of ddrextrm, ddr5m and
ddrmax2, docs/2026-10-30-music-level-and-announcer.md), and some players want them
quieter or gone while the arrows scroll. rtl/s573_voice_duck.v watches the SPU's
register writes (KEYON at 0x188/0x18A) and the Digital I/O MP3 state and marks the
voices keyed on inside the song window; this patch only applies that mask.

spu.vhd   : new inputs s573_duck(23:0) / s573_duck_mode(1:0). At VOICE_END a voice
            whose s573_duck bit is set is added to the dry mix AND the reverb send
            shifted right 1 (-6 dB) or 2 (-12 dB), or not at all (mode 11). Mode 00
            (the default, and the port default) takes the original path unchanged.
psx_top / psx_mister : pass-through of the two inputs, and the SPU's own bus port
            (bus_spu_write / bus_spu_addr / bus_spu_dataWrite) brought out as
            observation-only outputs. Stacks on 0031.

--- a/rtl/spu.vhd
+++ b/rtl/spu.vhd
@@ -82,7 +82,12 @@
       SS_RAM_request       : in  std_logic;
       SS_RAM_rnw           : in  std_logic;
       SS_RAM_dataRead      : out std_logic_vector(15 downto 0);
-      SS_RAM_done          : out std_logic
+      SS_RAM_done          : out std_logic;
+      -- System 573 (psx_patches 0035): per-voice attenuation for the OSD option
+      -- "573 Announcer/Crowd" (rtl/s573_voice_duck.v decides which voices).
+      -- duck_mode 00 = off (bit-exact upstream), 01 = -6 dB, 10 = -12 dB, 11 = mute.
+      s573_duck            : in  std_logic_vector(23 downto 0) := (others => '0');
+      s573_duck_mode       : in  std_logic_vector(1 downto 0) := "00"
    );
 end entity;
 
@@ -1835,6 +1840,28 @@
                   --end if;
                   
                when VOICE_END =>
+                  -- System 573 (psx_patches 0035): a ducked voice is added shifted
+                  -- (-6/-12 dB) or not at all, to the dry mix and the reverb send alike.
+                  if (s573_duck(index) = '1' and s573_duck_mode /= "00") then
+                     if (cnt(14) = '1') then -- mute voices
+                        case (s573_duck_mode) is
+                           when "01"   => soundleft  <= soundleft  + resize(shift_right(chanLeft , 1), 24);
+                                          soundright <= soundright + resize(shift_right(chanRight, 1), 24);
+                           when "10"   => soundleft  <= soundleft  + resize(shift_right(chanLeft , 2), 24);
+                                          soundright <= soundright + resize(shift_right(chanRight, 2), 24);
+                           when others => null;
+                        end case;
+                     end if;
+                     if (REVERBON(index) = '1') then
+                        case (s573_duck_mode) is
+                           when "01"   => reverbsumleft  <= reverbsumleft  + resize(shift_right(chanLeft , 1), 24);
+                                          reverbsumright <= reverbsumright + resize(shift_right(chanRight, 1), 24);
+                           when "10"   => reverbsumleft  <= reverbsumleft  + resize(shift_right(chanLeft , 2), 24);
+                                          reverbsumright <= reverbsumright + resize(shift_right(chanRight, 2), 24);
+                           when others => null;
+                        end case;
+                     end if;
+                  else
                   if (cnt(14) = '1') then -- mute voices
                      soundleft  <= soundleft  + resize(chanLeft , 24);
                      soundright <= soundright + resize(chanRight, 24);
@@ -1843,6 +1870,7 @@
                      reverbsumleft  <= reverbsumleft  + resize(chanLeft , 24);
                      reverbsumright <= reverbsumright + resize(chanRight, 24);
                   end if;
+                  end if;
                   
                   if (index = 1) then voice_lastVolume1 <= voice_lastVolume; end if;
                   if (index = 3) then voice_lastVolume3 <= voice_lastVolume; end if;
